Topic 1: Classes and objects

1.Class Definition, Object Instantiation

Definition:
Class Definition:
A class is a blueprint for creating objects.
It defines attributes (data) and methods (functions) common to all objects of that class.
Object Instantiation:
The process of creating an instance (object) of a class.
Each object has its own copy of attributes and can use methods defined by the class.
Syntax

class class_name:
    def __init__(self,p1,p2):
        self.p1 = p1
        self.p2 = p2
       
   
    def method_name(self):
        #Implementation of the method


Object_name=class_name(p1,p2)
object_name.method_name(self)

2.Class Attributes and Methods
Class Attributes:
Shared by all instances of the class.
Defined outside __init__ method.
Changes made to class attributes reflect across all instances.
Methods:
Operates on the instance (self). Can access both class and instance attributes.
3.Instance Variables vs. Class Variables
Class Attribute: Shared across all instances. Changes affect all instances.
Instance Attribute: Unique to each instance. Changes affect only that instance.
4.__init__ Constructor Method
Definition:
The __init__ method is a constructor in Python.
It is automatically invoked when a new object of the class is created.
It initializes instance attributes to specific values.
Syntax
class ClassName:
    def __init__(self, param1, param2, ...):
        # Initialize instance attributes
        self.attribute1 = param1
        self.attribute2 = param2

5.Self Parameter
Definition:
self is a reference to the current instance of the class.
It is used to access instance attributes and methods.
It allows each object to keep its own state.
Syntax
class ClassName:
    def method_name(self, param1, param2):
        self.attribute1 = param1
        self.attribute2 = param2

Memory Allocation of Objects
Definition:
Memory allocation is automatic in Python.
You don't need to specify memory size manually, unlike languages like C or C++.
Syntax
id() function can be used to get the memory address of an object:
print(id(object_name))







